    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d294">

                <pb facs="0382" n="374" sameAs="frus:frus1938v02/pg374"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.4016/1727: Telegram (part air)</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Austria</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Wiley</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Vienna</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-05-31T18:00:00+01:00">May 31, 1938—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 2—5 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>231. Since morning of 27th wholesale arrest of Jews. Many reported sent to
                    Dachau. Action reliably attributed to direct orders of Himmler<anchor n="35"
                        xml:id="d294-f1"/> and presumably intended further to demoralize Jews,
                    facilitate spoliation and expedite exodus.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wiley</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d294-f1" n="35" xml:id="d294-f1-content">
                <p>Heinrich Himmler, German Chief of the Schutzstaffeln and the Gestapo.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
